.TH GFAN 1 "2026-07-25" "gigactl 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfan \- control the fans on Gigabyte G5/G6 laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfan
.RI [ status ]
.br
.B gfan watch
.br
.B gfan auto
.br
.B gfan max
.br
.B gfan
.I percent
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B gfan
.I cpu-percent gpu-percent
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfan
reads and sets the two laptop fans through the Embedded Controller: fan 1 cools
the CPU, fan 2 the GPU. With no argument it prints temperatures, duty cycle and
RPM.
.PP
It works in one of two modes, chosen automatically each time it runs.
.TP
.B daemon
The
.BR gigactld (8)
service owns its D\-Bus name, which makes it the single writer of the Embedded
Controller.
.B gfan
becomes an unprivileged client of it: no
.BR sudo ,
no
.BR ec_probe ,
and no chance of the two interleaving controller commands. polkit lets the user
of the active local session do this without a password.
.TP
.B direct
No daemon is running, so
.B gfan
drives the controller itself and re\-runs itself under
.BR sudo (8)
to do so. Concurrent invocations take
.I /run/lock/gigactl\-ec.lock
\(em the same lock the daemon takes \(em so their command sequences cannot
interleave. This mode needs the
.B ec_probe
utility from nbfc\-linux.
.PP
If neither can be established \(em no
.BR busctl (1)
on the system, or the bus does not answer \(em
.B gfan
refuses to do anything rather than risk writing the controller behind a running
daemon's back.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print CPU and GPU temperature, each fan's duty cycle and RPM, and the current
mode. This is the default when no argument is given.
.TP
.B watch
Print the same status every two seconds until interrupted.
.TP
.B auto
Hand both fans back to the laptop firmware's own curve. A reboot does this too,
so no experiment can leave the fans stuck.
.TP
.B max
Run both fans at 100%.
.TP
.I percent
Run both fans at the given duty cycle, 0 to 100.
.TP
.I cpu-percent gpu-percent
Run fan 1 at the first duty cycle and fan 2 at the second.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow a duty cycle below 30% while the CPU is at or above 85 \(deC. Without it
such a request is refused, because slowing the fans down on an already hot
machine is the one combination that can cause damage rather than noise.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B gfan
exits 0 on success and 1 on failure: an unsupported machine, a refused duty
cycle, a controller that did not accept the write, a lock held by another
writer, or a daemon whose presence could not be determined.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GFAN_UNSAFE
Set to
.B 1
to skip the vendor and model check. The Embedded Controller protocol was
reverse engineered on a Gigabyte G6 KF; on hardware from another ODM the same
registers can mean anything at all, so overriding this risks the machine.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/gfan.mode
The manual duty cycle last set in direct mode, reported by
.BR "gfan status" .
Absent when the firmware is in control. Cleared on reboot.
.TP
.I /run/lock/gigactl\-ec.lock
Serialises Embedded Controller access between
.BR gfan ,
.BR gkbd (1)
and
.BR gigactld (8).
.SH NOTES
Verified on the Gigabyte G6 KF. Other G5, G6 and G7 models are expected to
work \(em they are the same Clevo\-ODM platform \(em and print a notice saying
they are untested. Anything else is refused.
.PP
In direct mode every duty cycle is read back after writing. If the controller
does not converge on the requested value,
.B gfan
hands the fans to the firmware and reports what happened, rather than leaving
them somewhere unintended. In daemon mode the daemon performs the same check.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gkbd (1),
.BR gigactl-gui (1),
.BR gigactld (8)
.PP
The reverse\-engineered controller protocol is documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/gigactl
and at
.UR https://github.com/smairio/gigactl
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
khalil Smairi
